{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>With whomever you find your gods, he shall not live.</b> Because of this ban Rachel was punished, that she died on the way. From this one learns that a person must take care regarding the punishment of the righteous and regarding their curse." "<b>Before our brethren, recognize for yourself what is mine and take for yourself.</b> This indicates the faith and the virtue of Jacob, and it is the way of the righteous that they do not covet the money of others, even of relatives. For Jacob, who dwelt in the house of his father-in-law twenty years and was blessed on his account, as Laban himself testified concerning him, נחשתי ויברכני ה׳ בגללך — I have divined and HaShem has blessed me on your account — would allow his father-in-law to enter all his tents, and any object that he recognized as his own he might take for himself; this is what he said: הכר לך מה עמדי וקח לך — recognize for yourself what is mine and take for yourself. And so he mentioned below: כי מששת את כל כלי מה מצאת מכל כלי ביתך — for you have groped all my vessels; what have you found of all the vessels of your house. Come and see how far the righteous distance themselves from robbery."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:42.958462593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}